    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "I added the \"period numbering from\" setting, and all 4 tests in the acceptance spec pass under `bin/e2e`.\n\n**How it behaves**\n- The Settings form has a new date field (`setting-period-numbering-from`) and a line showing the value in force (`setting-period-numbering-from-current`). Leaving it blank turns it off. Saving it writes `SETTING_CHANGED \u2026 key=period-numbering-from value=<date>`.\n- When a claim is opened while the setting is a date and the sheet's today is on or after it, the claim is numbered `<period name>-<n>`. The period is the one its date falls in, and each period counts from 1. A claim dated outside every period is numbered `X-<n>` in its own sequence. Otherwise it gets the next sheet-wide number. Claims opened earlier keep their numbers, and the sheet-wide count carries on from where it stopped once the setting is cleared.\n\n**Things that changed under the hood**\n- **Claim numbers are now text.** A claim's number, and the number a correction refers to, could only be whole numbers before. Now they can hold labels like `P1-1`, so a correction can name `X-1`. A new database migration, `V28__period_numbering.sql`, adds the setting and changes both columns to text. The \"Corrects claim no.\" field in the claim form now takes any value without spaces instead of digits only.\n- **How the next period number is found.** There's no stored counter per period. When a claim is opened, the app looks at the sheet's existing numbers that start with that period's name and takes the highest plus one. This runs with the sheet locked, so two claims opened at once can't get the same number.\n\n**Edge cases the tests don't cover**\n- A period actually named \"X\" would share its numbers with claims in no period.\n- If periods overlap, a claim is numbered in the one that starts earliest.\n\nThe server changes are in `ClaimService`, `Claim`, `Sheet`, `SheetService`, `PeriodService`, `SettingService`, `SettingController`, `ClaimController` and `RollupService`. The front-end changes are in the settings and claims features.",
